<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan grains/oilseeds tender results - February.</title>
<headline>Taiwan grains/oilseeds tender results - February.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan interests bought during February a total of 152,500 tonnes U.S. soybeans, 310,000 tonnes of U.S. corn, 54,000 tonnes of Argentine corn and 156,000 tonnes U.S. wheat at tenders.</p>
<p>The following table gives basic information on February</p>
<p>soybean/corn tender results, with the one Argentine shipment</p>
<p>marked **:</p>
<p>(Prices based on US$ per tonne)</p>
<p> Feb Buyer     Tonne  Type Delivery	 Seller  Price/Freight</p>
<p>  4  MFIG	27,000 corn Mar 20-April 4 Trady   $140.40/FOB</p>
<p>		   27,000 corn Mar 20-April 4 Trady   $.909/FOB</p>
<p> 19  BSPA	54,000 soy  Mar 16-30	Cargill $.10496/CNF</p>
<p> 19  FGEP	54,000 corn April 10-25    Zennoh  $.90</p>
<p> 20  MFIG   ** 54,000 corn April 10-30    Toepfer $.785</p>
<p> 25  BSPA-T    54,000 soy  Mar 21-April 4 Bunge   $.10766/CNF</p>
<p> 25  CK Group  54,000 corn April 11-25    Mitsui  $.5323/$14.28</p>
<p>25  CK Group  52,000 corn April 25-May 9 Mitsui  $.5223/$14.19</p>
<p>		    2,000 corn April 25-May 9 Mitsui  $134.45</p>
<p> 26  T. Sugar  24,000 corn April 10-25    Mitsui  $.5423/$20.90</p>
<p>		    6,000 soy  April 10-25    Mitsui  $.6653/$20.90</p>
<p> 27  Hui Shung 12,000 corn April 1-15     Cargill $150.00/CNF</p>
<p>		    4,000 corn April 1-15     Cargill $.9056/CNF</p>
<p>		   38,500 soy  April 1-15     Cargill $.10731</p>
<p> 27  MFIG	54,000 corn April 2-16     Mitsui  $150.00/CNF</p>
<p>Delivery periods for soybean and corn shipments are stated</p>
<p>for the U.S. Gulf Mexico. Shipments from the Pacific Northwest</p>
<p>are 15 days after the Gulf.</p>
<p>==============================================================</p>
